Title: "Realizes"
Id: "812d2a6f-e574-4328-9454-637b8e39340c"

Text: "`Realizes:` supplies a concrete implementation for every component left open
by a `Defines:` item marked `abstractly:`.

```mlg-fragment
[CommandHeader]
Realizes: <DeclarationStatement>
using?: <DeclarationStatement>+
when?: <ClauseUnion>+
specifies?: <IsOrViaItem>+
expresses?: <ClauseUnion>+
Requires?: <RequiresItemUnion>+
Enables?: <EnablesItemUnion>+
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

The target has the form `<subject> := <abstract command>`. The right side must
resolve to an abstract `Defines:` item, not a `Declares:` type.

```mlg-fragment
[\von.neumann.naturals]
Realizes: Nb := \naturals
specifies:
. N := \von.neumann.omega
. 0 := \empty.set
. succ(n_) := n_ \union \set@{n_}
Documented:
. called: \"von Neumann natural number system\"
```

Component types and capabilities are inherited from the abstract definition.
The realization must supply every open component, may not invent a component,
and may use `expresses:` for a callable body. Direct component access on a
realization uses `..`, just as for an ordinary `Defines:` command."
Id: "91d8f06f-3097-4268-8a53-d0d2027e942e"
